ADDENDA <Presidential Decree No. 34584, Jun. 18, 2024>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Decree shall enter into force on July 3, 2024; provided, the amended provisions of each of the following subparagraphs shall begin to apply on the date specified in the relevant subparagraph:
1. The amended provisions of subparagraph 1 of Article 5: July 19, 2024;
2. The amended provisions of subparagraph 1-2 of Article 5: October 17, 2024.
Article 2 (Deadline for preparation and submission of responsibilities map)
"Period prescribed by Presidential Decree" in subparagraph 4 of Article 6 of the Addenda to the partially amended Act on Corporate Governance of Financial Companies (Act No. 19913) means the period as classified in the following subparagraphs:
1. Financial investment business entities under Article 2(1)b of the Act (excluding those falling under subparagraph 2 of Article 6 of the Addenda to the partially amended Act on Corporate Governance of Financial Companies (Act No. 19913)): 2 years after the enforcement date of this Decree;
2. Insurance companies under Article 2(1)c of the Act (excluding those falling under subparagraph 3 of Article 6 of the Addenda to the partially amended Act on Corporate Governance of Financial Companies (Act No. 19913)): 2 years after the enforcement date of this Decree;
3. Mutual savings banks under Article 2(1)d of the Act: The period as classified in the following items:
a. Mutual savings banks whose total assets as of the end of the immediately preceding business year in which the enforcement date of this Decree falls are not less than 700 billion won: 2 years after the enforcement date of this Decree;
b. Mutual savings banks other than those referred to in item a: 3 years after the enforcement date of this Decree;
4. Specialized credit finance companies under Article 2(1)e of the Act: The period as classified in the following items:
a. Specialized credit finance companies whose total assets as of the end of the immediately preceding business year in which the enforcement date of this Decree falls are not less than 5 trillion won: 2 years after the enforcement date of this Decree;
b. Specialized credit finance companies other than those referred to in item a: 3 years after the enforcement date of this Decree;
5. Financial companies under Article 2(1)g of the Act: 6 months after the enforcement date of this Decree.
Article 3 (Applicability to scope of finance-related statutes or regulations)
(1) Regarding the provisions on the qualification requirements for executive officers, compliance officers, and risk management officers under Articles 5, 26, and 28 of the Act, the amended provisions of Article 5 shall begin to apply where an executive officer, compliance officer, or risk management officer of a financial company is appointed (including re-appointment) after the enforcement date of this Decree; provided, for those currently in office as an executive officer, compliance officer, or risk management officer as of the enforcement date of this Decree, the amended provisions shall begin to apply, limited to their term of office, to violations of statutes or regulations under the amended provisions of Article 5 after the enforcement date of this Decree.
(2) Regarding the provisions on the qualification review of the largest shareholder under Article 32 of the Act, the amended provisions of Article 5 shall begin to apply to the examination of whether the requirements for maintaining eligibility are met after the enforcement date of this Decree; provided, for those subject to the fitness and propriety assessment under Article 32(1) of the Act as of the enforcement date of this Decree (excluding those who cease to be subject to an eligibility review after the enforcement date of this Decree and later become subject to an fitness and propriety assessment again), the amended provisions shall begin to apply to violations of statutes or regulations under the amended provisions of Article 5 after the enforcement date of this Decree.
Article 4 (Transitional measures concerning internal control committee chaired by chief executive officer)
An internal control committee chaired by a chief executive officer established in a financial company under the previous Article 19(2) before the enforcement date of this Decree shall, notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 19(2), continue to exist within the limit of 1 year from the enforcement date of this Decree until an internal control committee within the board of directors under subparagraph 5 of Article 16(1) of the Act is established.

